MOTION FOR LEAVE TO ANSWER AND ANSWER OF  
NORTHERN VIRGINIA ELECTRIC COOPERATIVE, INC.  
TO THE AUGUST 18, 2026, MOTION FOR LEAVE TO ANSWER AND ANSWER OF 
VISTRA CORP. 

Pursuant to Rules 212 and 213 of the Rules of Practice and Procedure of the Federal Energy 
Regulatory Commission (“FERC” or the “Commission”),1 Northern Virginia Electric 
Cooperative, Inc. (“NOVEC”) respectfully submits this Motion for Leave to Answer and Answer 
to the August 18, 2026, Motion for Leave to Answer and Answer of Vistra Corp. (“Vistra”)2 filed 
in response to NOVEC’s Motion for Clarification3 of the Commission’s June 18, 2026, Order in 
these consolidated dockets.4 

1 18 C.F.R. § 385.212-213. 
2 Vistra Corp., Motion for Leave to Answer and Answer, Docket Nos. EL25-49-000, et al. (Aug. 18, 2026) 
(Accession No. 20260818-5146) (“August 18 Answer”). 
3 NOVEC, Motion for Clarification, Docket Nos. EL25-49-000, et al. (Jul. 29, 2026) (Accession No. 20260729-
5083) (“July 29 Motion for Clarification”).  
4 PJM Interconnection, L.L.C., 195 FERC ¶ 61,209 (2026) (“Order”).
